"Internal Error ()\nciteturn6498view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15894v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15894v1: Cache miss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2512.15931v1] BarcodeMamba+: Advancing State-Space Models for Fungal Biodiversity Research (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15931v1)\nciteturn6498view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15931v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 165\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 17 Dec 2025]\nL9: # Title:BarcodeMamba+: Advancing State-Space Models for Fungal Biodiversity Research\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Tiancheng Gao , cite6†Scott C. Lowe , cite7†Brendan Furneaux , cite8†Angel X Chang , cite9†Graham W. Taylor L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled BarcodeMamba+: Advancing State-Space Models for Fungal Biodiversity Research, by Tiancheng Gao and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite10†View PDF cite11†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Accurate taxonomic classification from DNA barcodes is a cornerstone of global biodiversity monitoring, yet fungi present extreme challenges due to sparse labelling and long-tailed taxa distributions. Conventional supervised learning methods often falter in this domain, struggling to generalize to unseen species and to capture the hierarchical nature of the data.\nL17: To address these limitations, we introduce BarcodeMamba+, a foundation model for fungal barcode classification built on a powerful and efficient state-space model architecture. We employ a pretrain and fine-tune paradigm, which utilizes partially labelled data and we demonstrate this is substantially more effective than traditional fully-supervised methods in this data-sparse environment.\nL18: During fine-tuning, we systematically integrate and evaluate a suite of enhancements--including hierarchical label smoothing, a weighted loss function, and a multi-head output layer from MycoAI--to specifically tackle the challenges of fungal taxonomy. Our experiments show that each of these components yields significant performance gains.\nL19: On a challenging fungal classification benchmark with distinct taxonomic distribution shifts from the broad training set, our final model outperforms a range of existing methods across all taxonomic levels. Our work provides a powerful new tool for genomics-based biodiversity research and establishes an effective and scalable training paradigm for this challenging domain. Our code is publicly available at cite12†this https URL†github.com .\nL20: Comments:  | 11 pages, accepted at the 3rd Workshop on Imageomics: Discovering Biological Knowledge from Images Using AI (NeurIPS 2025)\nL21: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite13†arXiv:2512.15931 [cs.LG]\nL23:    | (or cite14†arXiv:2512.15931v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL24:    | cite15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2512.15931†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Tiancheng Gao [cite16†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Wed, 17 Dec 2025 19:56:03 UTC (75 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled BarcodeMamba+: Advancing State-Space Models for Fungal Biodiversity Research, by Tiancheng Gao and 4 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite10†View PDF L37:   * cite11†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite17†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite18†view license†creativecommons.org L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.LG\nL44: \nL45: cite19†< prev |   cit